PLAN=plan(5,'Percentages and applications','Part II · Parts and proportions',14,'Fairness and development','Quantity, Proportion','Percentages express change and comparison relative to a whole; identifying that whole makes financial and fairness decisions more reliable.','Two shops advertise different discount sequences. Which offer is genuinely cheaper, and what must a price card make clear?','In order for a student to think critically, students must identify the reference quantity, test a claim with calculations and explain the limits of a financial decision.',S,explore,application,assessment,mixed,ready,check,[S[0]['diagram'],S[2]['diagram']],['Convert between fractions, decimals and percentages.','Find percentages and percentage changes.','Use multipliers for successive changes.','Interpret discounts, taxes, costs and profit in a budget.'],'per cent · reference amount · multiplier · percentage change · discount · tax · revenue · cost · gross profit · net profit',key='Change',sourcepages='95–113; answers 225–227')
